sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor T as Trainer
    actor S as Student
    participant AS as assessment-service
    participant BA as batch-service
    participant K as Kafka
    participant RP as reporting-service

    T->>AS: create test (DRAFT): questions, pool size, shuffle, attempts, duration
    T->>AS: publish
    AS->>AS: DRAFT -> PUBLISHED (a published test cannot be edited)

    S->>AS: POST /api/quizzes/{id}/attempts
    AS->>BA: is the student in the batch? (Feign)
    AS->>AS: attempts used < attempts_allowed + extra for this student?
    alt allowance used up
        AS-->>S: refused
    else may start
        AS->>AS: draw this attempt's questions from the pool, keep the ids
        AS->>AS: shuffle questions and options per student
        AS-->>S: paper (no answer key), deadline, saved answers if resuming
    end

    loop while answering
        S->>AS: PUT /quiz-attempts/{id}/answers (autosave)
        AS->>AS: write only changed answers
    end

    alt student submits
        S->>AS: POST /quiz-attempts/{id}/submit
    else time runs out
        AS->>AS: AttemptExpiryJob settles it, status EXPIRED
    end
    AS->>AS: score on the server from the stored key (coding uses stored verdicts)
    AS->>K: quiz-attempt-completed
    K->>RP: progress and dashboard facts
    S->>AS: GET /quiz-attempts/{id}/result
    AS-->>S: marks, pass or fail, review if allowed
    T->>AS: results sheet: violations, pasted-code note, +1 attempt for one student
